  "hypothesis": "Unmapped Quaternary Basin-and-Range normal faults and blind geothermal upflow conduits concentrated in low-relief (<6 deg) piedmont aprons and intrabasinal step-overs \u2014 where 52.6% of mapped faults sit and 100 m DEM smoothing erases 1-3 m scarps \u2014 are recoverable by coupling seamless USGS 3DEP 10 m sub-pixel scarp excess/curvature/coherence and 10 m channel chi/k_sn steps with tufa-filtered DOE GDR #1391 INGENIOUS paleo-geothermal sinter/Qss/explosion vents, 2-m shallow temperature probe anomalies (2mDAB), active thermal springs, and GeoDAWN K/Th, U/Th, and TMI_up150-RTP shallow magnetite-destruction residuals.",
  "mechanism": "4-quadrant Leave-One-Quadrant-Out (LOQO, >=1.2 km guard band, >500 m negative buffer, zero fault-catalogue inputs) HistGradientBoostingClassifier ensemble over 26 physical features (Group A: 8 USGS 3DEP 10 m sub-pixel scarp & chi-step features; Group B: 9 tufa-filtered INGENIOUS hydrothermal vent, 2mDAB, K/Th, U/Th & Grauch demagnetization features; Group C: 9 province-debiased gravity/basement/strain & Lake Lahontan shoreline-null features), calibrated within quadrants and localized onto 37,654 Poisson-spaced 1D crests (min_dist=3.1 px, d_cat>2.0 px).",
  "non_fault_mimic": "Pleistocene pluvial Lake Lahontan shoreline tufa towers (86 Tufa records in Paleo_geothermal_final.csv explicitly excluded) and ~1,330 m Sehoo wave-cut beach berms (deconfounded via cross-contour transgression and shoreline-null index), plus non-tectonic alpine talus chutes cancelled by sub-pixel scarp excess log1p(S_10m) - log1p(S_100m).",
